.Dd November 20, 2026
.Dt RUN-CUDA-LLAMA.SH 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm run-cuda-llama.sh
.Nd run the llama.cpp CUDA build on the NVIDIA GPU through the Linuxulator
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar PROG
.Op Ar args ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Runs a program from the official llama.cpp
.Pa ubuntu-cuda-13.5-arm64
release (with the cudart and cuBLAS libraries from the matching cudart asset
merged into the same directory) against NVIDIA's Linux libcuda, through the
Linuxulator, with the CUDA shim preloaded and the Ubuntu 24.04 glibc loader.
The kernel side is nvidia.ko and uvm-bsd.
.Pp
.Ar PROG
is a program in the release directory, for example
.Nm llama-bench ,
.Nm llama-cli
or
.Nm llama-server .
The script changes into that directory first, because ggml finds its backend
libraries next to the loader and in the current directory only.
Pass absolute model paths.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width ".Ev GB10_WORK"
.It Ev GB10_WORK
Work root, default
.Pa $HOME/work/gb10 .
.It Ev LL
The release directory, default
.Pa $GB10_WORK/llm/cuda/llama-b12531-cuda/llama-b12531 .
.It Ev SHIMDIR
Directory with
.Pa shim.so ,
default
.Pa $GB10_WORK/build/linux-cuda .
.El
.Pp
.Ev GGML_BACKEND_PATH
is unset, because it names one backend library and stops ggml from loading the others.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
The exit status of
.Ar PROG ;
2 for a usage error or no
.Ev HOME ;
1 when a required file is missing.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Dl run-cuda-llama.sh llama-bench --list-devices
.Dl run-cuda-llama.sh llama-bench -m /home/me/work/models/m.gguf -ngl 99 -fa 1
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr bench-report.sh 1 ,
.Xr run-nv-vulkan.sh 1
